stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 15 TL 60 740 Td
(3. Deployment and Scaling) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In production the service is deployed as Docker containers orchestrated by Kubernetes.) Tj T*
(Each component runs in its own Kubernetes deployment. For single-server installations, see) Tj T*
(the Installation Guide.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Inventory API runs a minimum of 2 replicas. A Horizontal Pod Autoscaler scales it from) Tj T*
(2 to 10 replicas when average CPU usage exceeds 70 percent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Releases use rolling updates with maxUnavailable set to 0, so deployments cause no) Tj T*
(downtime.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Configuration is supplied through Kubernetes ConfigMaps, and credentials through) Tj T*
(Kubernetes Secrets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A liveness probe calls GET /api/v1/health every 10 seconds; a pod is restarted after 3) Tj T*
(failed checks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Disaster recovery: restore the latest PostgreSQL backup. The recovery point objective is) Tj T*
(24 hours and the recovery time objective is 4 hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
